-*   **Input:** A set of $N$ 3D points $P = \{p_1, p_2, \dots, p_N\}$ representing Voronoi sites or data vertices.
-*   **Output:** A set of tetrahedra $T$, where each tetrahedron is defined by 4 vertices from $P$.
